hey everyone bandit here the other day i  made a community post right here on  youtube about fam theories that you may  have that none of the zelda theorists  have covered yet and i made a video  about it and turns out it was actually a  really good idea that most of you really  enjoyed watching so thank you so much  for the positive reactions and if you  haven't gotten a chance to check it out  yet i'll leave a link in the description  below but i wanted to bring attention to  one comment that i saw in particular  that was just too big to not receive a  dedicated video it's a breath of the  wild sequel theory from a user named  jaden everett now the theory that he  brings up is actually what i'm going to  cover in this video so i won't show the  comment on the screen in its entirety at  this time but please feel free to head  over to the comments of the community  post and leave a like on jaden's comment  to show him some support after the video  between reading jaden's comment and  talking it over with one of my good  friends and discord server moderators  named lonline historian who had a lot to  bring to the table i think this theory  has some very decent believability and  it's all about ganondorf and the master  sword but probably not like what you're  thinking see pretty much everyone at  this point has pointed out that as of  the second breath of the wild sequel  trailer link has been shown doing  several new things like falling through  the sky or shooting flames out of a  shield attachment on his  shield or having malice grapple onto his  arm and as i'm sure you all remember  that last nasty malice one was the only  time in the second trailer that link was  shown with the master sword all of his  appearances afterwards be it in hyrule  or skyrule are master sword less and  sure it could just be a case of link  using other weapons as the master sword  could just be chilling in his inventory  you know recharging but i think it's  more deliberate than that see ever since  the first trailer to the sequel when  zelda and link were exploring that  mysterious dank cave link has been shown  with the master sword deliberately like  in every shot and then similarly the  first thing you see in the new trailer  is again link with the master sword  deliberately but then never again in  every other shot in the trailer to me as  i said in a previous video that i did  with mr celtic who's actually a really  cool guy by the way i think this implies  that link loses the master sword and i  think it happens when ling's arm gets  grappled onto and corrupted by that  malice which we can see has literally  changed his arm's appearance for the  remainder of the trailer well either  that or the green power that grapples  onto it in the first trailer but that's  besides the point clearly link survives  this encounter and i'm sure that's what  the events of the game are largely going  to cover but the thing is if the master  sword isn't with our blonde hero for the  events of the game it must still be  chilling back in that cave with  ganondorf who we can't forget was shown  to be standing with his arms stretched  outwards almost triumphantly in the new  trailer as if things were all going  according to plan the question is what  plan if ganondorf did take the master  sword from link what exactly is he going  to do with it could he even do anything  to it great questions i'm so glad you  all asked because i can't answer any of  them for sure but we can speculate let  us now rewind from the latest game in  the timeline breath of the wild all the  way back to the first game in the  timeline skyward sword back to the birth  of the master sword to quickly recap  what happens to the master sword in the  game basically it starts out as a highly  afforded blade known as the goddess  sword and then gets tempered by the  flames of din faror and nehru and then  blessed by the mortal incarnation of  hylia also known as zelda in order to  transform fully into the true master  sword complete with the power to repel  evil actually it's more like the power  to contain evil see link takes up the  sword and at the end of the game after  girihim pulls some time shenanigans and  takes their fight into the past ends up  fighting the big bad og demon king  himself demise not only does link fight  demise he kills him well kind of that's  actually kind of questionable here  because demise doesn't go up dead like a  normal person he instead does this sort  of thanos snap dissolve into thin air  thing and gets absorbed into the master  sword directly the spirit that resides  in the sword that goes by a name that i  refuse to pronounce at this time even  confirms this and states that she has  confirmed the eradication of the demon  king whose residual consciousness has  been absorbed into the master sword and  is now sealed away but notice they never  once state that demise has died actually  he wasn't completely gone which i think  is key here impa even confirms this  later on and says that the last remnants  of demise are slowly decaying within the  master sword and she even elects to stay  behind and watch over the sword because  of this out of fear that he might  actually break out of his seal since he  still exists so here's the next question  to ask if the biggest and baddest dude  ever known in the history of the zelda  universe is not actually dead yet and is  still alive within the master sword  might this have some sort of impact on  the sword well yes it just might  actually and this is where jaden's  comment really starts to shine see he  theorizes that demise's intense demonic  essence even though it was in a weakened  state was still very much so alive and  was actually causing the master sword in  turn to weaken this is why skyward  strikes are no longer a thing following  demise's entry into the sword at the end  of skyrid's sword and it's also why the  master sword appears to now have a  tendency of slowly fading in potency  over time having to routinely be  re-empowered back to its original state  in games like the wind waker or a link  between worlds or most recently breath  of the wild it is a bit strange that the  perfect seemingly omnipotent blade of  evil's bane created by hylia herself  would continually tend to lose its touch  wouldn't you say but i know what you're  thinking what does all of this have to  do with ganondorf in the trailer for  breath of the wild too hold your loft  wings i'm getting there so we talked  about the master sword containing the  very essence of the original most  powerful of all demon kings right and  we've talked about how demise's essence  is probably still living within the  sword as proven by its slow drain over  time now let's bring it back to this  scene in the cave of the breath of the  wild sequel haven't you felt that  something's off here i know something  evil is about to happen but haven't you  felt that something very very wrong is  about to happen maybe it's something  about the music or the fact that  everything is so different but i can't  help feeling that something may happen  so terrifying that it may shatter all of  our expectations and even the very  foundations of the zelda metanarrative  as we know it after the incarnation of  his malice the dark beast ganon was  ultimately defeated and his plan stopped  for what must be the hundredth or  thousandth time what if ganondorf  decided he's had enough and that he's  out to change the cycle forever what if  ganondorf knows that demise exists  within the blade and he took it from  link in order to release the essence of  the original demon king from within the  sword in order to fuse with his own  power and create a darkness the likes of  which the world has never seen this is  what jaden's comment was about i've  theorized before that the master swords  breaking may be necessary to finally  stop the cycling curse of the demon  tribe which is as good a theory as any  other but that was implying that  breaking it would destroy demise what if  instead breaking it would release him of  course ganondorf being able to break the  master sword is something that you  wouldn't think is possible at first but  what if he doesn't have to break it what  if instead he could somehow coax the  essence of demise out of the blade by  using dark magic all he really needed  was to separate the blade from link and  remove zelda from the picture both of  which he's done will ganondorf terrorize  hyrule worse than ever before with the  full power of demise at his disposal who  knows after all it's just a neat theory  from a couple of awesome zelda theorists  named jaden everett and law online  historian personally i look forward to  finding out in 2022 if nintendo keeps to  that release schedule  but until then what did you guys think  about this theory let me know in the  comments below and let me know if you  have a theory that you'd like me to  check out and potentially cover as well  also to all of you listening to my voice  right now thank you thank you so much  for watching and if i could ask  something of you real quick would you be  so kind as to leave a like on this video  if you liked this video and subscribe to  the channel if you haven't already in  order to stick around for much more  nintendo content to come it takes two  seconds and you can always unsubscribe  later also huge thanks to my bandit crew  who make my day every single day if you  watching are interested in helping these  videos come to life and helping an  internet weirdo like myself buy some  chicken nuggies for my rumbling tummies  please feel free to check out that join  button located below any of my videos or  the patreon and merch pages in the  description below also down there are  the links to my social media pages so  come on over and follow me on twitter or  instagram for some colorful insights  that's all i've got for this one so as  always i hope you have a wonderfu